WEBVTT

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.310
Good morning!

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.190
Good morning.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.770
Good morning, Teacher!

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.280
Good morning.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.670
Make sure to try hard in today's duels!

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:25.740
Okay!

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.260
Lua!  Luca!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.570
Aki!

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:29.680
Good morning.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.070
Aki, I heard you have the 
high school's best grades.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.460
Awesome!

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:39.000
I'm going to be just like Aki and become 
the elementary school's top student!

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.010
I did it!

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:49.230
Lua, if I was grading your 
reactions, you'd get 100%.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.300
Sheesh, you're just all talk.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.200
Weren't you going to become the top student?

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:56.670
I can't fight with this deck.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:02.610
If I had this one turn earlier, I 
could've summoned Power Tool Dragon!

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.930
Shame on you!  You included 
your favorite card again?

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.320
This lesson is about Warrior-Type decks.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.580
C'mon, I'm stronger when I include 
Machine-Type monsters in my deck.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.000
Lua, duel me next!

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.290
Lua, duel me!

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:18.770
I'll duel Patty after Bob!

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.040
Am I popular?

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.430
Of course not.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.170
Our grades go up when we duel you.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.500
What do you mean by that!

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:36.140
You stupid kids won't be 
having fun for much longer!

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:01.080
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:06.620
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:11.090
Don't look back and keep going

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:16.930
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.900
There's no need to fear

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:29.580
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.580
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.350
Streak to the infinite future

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:46.760
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:54.870
And will lead you to a bright place

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:27.100
Duel Academy's Tradition!Ancient Gear Golem

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.620
Lua!

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.480
Are you going there today?

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.030
Yeah.  You're coming too, right?

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.410
We're coming!

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:39.530
Lua, aren't you bothering them 
if you're going everyday?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.030
It's fine.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.030
Sly.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.370
Are you going home alone?

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.540
Sly, want to come with us?

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.130
What a group.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.010
You should just go straight home.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:52.960
Sly...

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.980
I don't like his attitude.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.980
He's a little different.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:00.300
Let's hurry up and go to Yusei's place!

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.850
Yeah!  I want to meet Yusei!

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.390
What?  Yusei?

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:09.360
They're going to Yusei Fudo's place…

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.300
Output is at 80… 90…

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.000
Is this safe?

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.740
I don't want another 
explosion like last time.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.820
Impressive, Yusei!

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:27.710
You've perfected it in only a few days.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.860
Yeah, at least there's no 
problem with the engine...

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:30.950
Engine?

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:31.950
"At least?"

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:37.250
The cards!

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.430
Be quiet!

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:44.200
How many disturbances are you going to cause?

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.530
I don't know if you're making 
things or breaking things!

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.670
I'm sorry.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.900
Don't blame Yusei.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.500
That's right.  You'll be 
doing Jack Atlas a favor.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.110
I was talking about you 
two from the beginning!

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.340
Zora, I'm really sorry.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.390
It's fine, Yusei.

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.210
How unfortunate for you.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:07.400
You should occasionally take a break instead 
of working on that machine all the time.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:13.320
You two should help Yusei 
instead of holding him back!

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:16.430
How dare she treat us so differently!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:21.720
I prefer that she yells at me instead 
of giving me that eerie insincere smile.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.110
Don't say that.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:25.400
Zora is letting us stay here.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.830
I guess...

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.050
Anyway...

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.480
We have to do something about this.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.360
Yusei!  Jack!  Crow!

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.880
We came to visit!

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.550
Welcome!

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:36.610
Again?

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.250
It's messy again, as usual.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:41.550
What happened?  Another explosion?

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:42.620
Sorta.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:45.090
We hurt its feelings.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:47.060
It's a D-Wheel!

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.690
Wow!

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:50.050
It's a frame for testing purposes.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:51.030
Cool!

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.500
Don't touch it!

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.080
Let me ride it!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:55.930
Can we?

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.390
No!  Have you no shame?

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:02.200
If you help pick up the 
cards, we'll let you ride!

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.050
Really?

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.510
Crow!  You can't decide that on your own!

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.210
It's fine.  Let's start!

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.830
Yusei, we'll help too.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:12.840
Thank you.

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.730
Sly.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:17.240
Why is he here?

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:18.220
Sly!

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:19.610
Sly!

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.530
What are you doing?  Come over here.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:25.900
Yusei, he's our classmate!

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.560
He's really strong.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.890
Right, Sly?

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.090
Nice to meet you.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.160
So you're Yusei Fudo.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.680
Just as I thought, you're not very cool.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.620
What?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.010
Why aren't you working?

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.500
Get back to work!

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.780
Why do I have to do this?

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.580
That's…

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.040
Stardust Dragon.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.330
It should be around here.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.880
Here it is.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.020
Thank you.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.380
Are you Yusei Fudo?

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.580
Yes.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.320
I heard that you can fix anything.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:17.380
What did you break?

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:22.240
It's not broken.  It's out-of-control.

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:27.180
I think you can fix it if 
you tighten the screws.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.830
Tighten the screws?

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.690
What kind of machine are you talking about?

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:34.520
It's called Heitmann.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.960
Heitmann?

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.460
Silence!

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:43.170
No matter what you say, 
it's already been decided!

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.860
Why is this happening?

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.380
Why are we expelled?

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:50.590
Relative to other schools, this 
school's academic performance

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:52.890
has greatly dropped this semester!

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:58.120
Duel Academy is the model school in Neo 
Domino City!  This isn't acceptable!

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:03.180
Therefore, the lowest level's 
loser class will be shut down!

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.390
Vice Principal, you've gone too far!

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:10.300
The principal always says that every 
child has the right to study dueling!

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:14.410
The principal has already agreed.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.110
What?  The principal?

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:22.350
That carefree principal finally 
understood my way of teaching.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.780
I can't believe that the 
principal would agree!

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:29.120
Please don't expel us!

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.790
I want to work hard with everyone!

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:32.490
This is too much!

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:36.890
None of you have the right 
to say that, especially Lua!

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.290
You have the lowest grades out of everyone!

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:42.900
Aki!

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:45.870
Oh my, you're Aki Izayoi.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.190
You consider yourself a teacher?

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:50.520
Why are you angry?

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:57.100
I thought an excellent student 
like you would endorse my views.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:01.090
I'll never forgive an 
adult who hurts children!

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:02.040
Aki!

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:05.720
This is bad.  If he makes Aki angry…

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:06.690
What's wrong, Aki?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.960
Yusei?

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:12.630
You're Yusei Fudo, the 
winner of the Fortune Cup!

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:17.500
Why are you here at Duel Academy?

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.070
I'm here to work.

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:21.270
Work?

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.980
There's something in this classroom that 
needs to be fixed, and I accepted the job.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:30.810
What needs to be fixed in this classroom?

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:33.980
Even these kids' grades can't be fixed.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:36.690
Vice Principal, that's 
a horrible thing to say!

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:40.360
It's foolish to judge them 
solely on their grades

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:43.660
and ignore their desire 
to learn about dueling!

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:45.660
You're the foolish one!

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:51.110
There's no point for low-level 
losers to learn about dueling!

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:56.550
Besides, these kids only have low-Level 
garbage monsters in their decks.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:01.910
Since their dueling skills are low, 
they can only use low-Level monsters.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.280
No, that's wrong.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:06.980
Nothing in this world is useless.

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:08.990
Stop acting so righteous!

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:11.940
An outsider has no right to interfere!

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.860
Hurry up and go home!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.890
What did you come here to fix?

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:21.140
I came here to fix something called Heitmann.

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:23.130
Heitmann?

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:23.970
Yeah.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:26.550
I can fix it by tightening its screws.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.870
Are you talking about me?  Rudolph Heitmann?

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:32.640
What?

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:34.320
Yusei, save us!

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.160
He's going to expel us!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.850
Please!

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:40.650
Do something, Yusei!

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:42.790
I see.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:44.320
I get it.

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:48.630
I'll fulfill your wishes!

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:51.290
Heitmann, duel me!

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:54.870
If I win, you won't expel them!

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:56.890
How impudent!

00:10:56.890 --> 00:11:01.830
I'll teach you that losers 
have no right to duel!

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:02.940
Got it?

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:05.670
Will he be okay?

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:08.650
The vice principal's deck is powerful.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.650
Don't worry.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:14.200
If you let Yusei handle it, he'll fix it.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.500
Do your best, Yusei.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.990
Defeat the vice principal!

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.500
Leave it to me.

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:23.590
But I have a favor to ask.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:25.800
A favor?

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:34.060
I'll use my ultimate victory deck 
to show you something incredible!

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:36.960
Duel!

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:52.480
Duel!

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.860
Yusei!  Do your best!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:55.890
Yusei!

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.360
I go first!

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.540
I draw!

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.380
I summon Flamvell Guard in defense position!

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:07.010
Do your best, Flamvell Guard!

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:09.130
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:12.170
A Level 1 monster?

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:16.010
You can only summon a 
low-Level Tuner Monster?

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:18.850
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:23.630
It's here!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:27.850
I summon Ancient Gear Statue!

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:34.060
I'll use this Level 2 monster 
to give you a special lesson.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.090
Special lesson?

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:37.790
Yes, that's right.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:42.450
No matter how many low-Level monsters 
you summon, you can't win this duel.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:45.310
There's a proper way to 
use low-Level monsters.

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:48.650
This is how you use them!

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:52.430
I activate the spell card 
Machine Duplication!

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:56.110
I select a Machine-Type monster 
with 500-or-fewer attack points.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:13:02.060
I can Special Summon two Ancient 
Gear Statues from my deck!

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:04.030
He has three copies of the same monster!

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:07.660
I activate Ancient Gear Statues' effects!

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:11.340
By releasing these monsters, I can ignore

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:16.040
Ancient Gear Golems' summoning 
requirements and Special Summon them!

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:17.210
What?

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:30.950
They look incredible!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.430
3000 attack points!

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:34.290
And three of them at once!

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:39.540
Even veteran duelists have 
never seen Ancient Gear Golem!

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.340
It's a legendary rare card!

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:45.370
But why does the vice principal 
have such an incredible card?

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:53.050
Only certain elite teachers at Duel Academy 
are allowed to use this vintage monster!

00:13:53.050 --> 00:14:00.950
Low-Level monsters are only useful when 
they're sacrificed to bring out high-Level monsters.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:08.220
Similarly, you low-level duelists are only 
useful when you're sacrificed to the elite!

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:10.770
That's enough.

00:14:10.770 --> 00:14:15.030
You can summon the most powerful monsters, 
but it's pointless if you can't win!

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:18.740
You're supposed to make excuses 
after you lose, not before.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:24.090
How can you win in this situation?

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.940
I activate a trap before the battle!

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.680
Tuner's Barrier!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:33.460
My Tuner Monster can't be 
destroyed in battle this turn!

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:36.670
That's low-level resistance.

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:42.490
When Ancient Gear Golem attacks a monster in 
defense position, you take piercing damage!

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:43.720
Battle!

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:48.330
The first Ancient Gear Golem 
attacks Flamvell Guard!

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:54.740
Next, the second Ancient Gear Golem attacks!

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:58.810
I'm not done!

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:03.400
The third Ancient Gear Golem attacks!

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:10.130
He instantly lost 3000 life points!

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:11.610
Yusei!

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:13.360
I'll finish you with this!

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:16.300
I activate the spell card Level Thunder!

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:21.590
You take damage equal to the total Level 
of my monsters multiplied by 100 points.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:24.230
Ancient Gear Golem is Level 8.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.590
Since he has three, it's Level 24.

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:29.070
That means it's all over.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:31.430
He'll take 2400 points of damage!

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.080
Yusei is going to lose?

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.250
I never knew this combo!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:43.430
Only a high-Level elite can 
execute this one turn kill!

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.530
Yusei!

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:46.190
Yusei!

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:50.390
By discard Hanewata from my 
hand, effect damage becomes 0!

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.130
Hooray!  Hanewata is great!

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:56.990
Another low-Level Tuner Monster?

00:15:56.990 --> 00:16:00.580
You have the stamina of a cockroach.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.040
I end my turn.

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:05.240
He managed to survive, but at this rate…

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.710
Yusei…

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:10.370
It's my turn to give you a special lesson.

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:14.970
These kids aren't low-level duelists!

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:16.910
I'll teach you that!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.490
That's absurd!

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:22.480
I have three Level 8 Ancient Gear Golems.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:26.010
You only have one Level 1 Tuner Monster.

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:29.500
What can you teach me in this situation?

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.610
My turn!

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:34.730
I activate the spell card 
Cards of Consonance!

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:40.210
By sending one Tuner Monster in my hand 
to the graveyard, I get to draw two cards!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:43.640
You're allowed to use Tuners like that?

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:46.160
I drew it.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:49.650
I summon Eccentric Boy!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:55.440
If I use Eccentric Boy to Synchro Summon, 
I select the other monster from my hand.

00:16:56.150 --> 00:17:00.830
Level 3 Eccentric Boy tunes 
Level 5 Turret Warrior!

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:06.020
What?  You're tuning a monster in your hand?

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:11.070
The wishes come together 
to form a new shining star!

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:12.840
Become the path that lights the way!

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:15.180
Synchro Summon!

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.010
Soar, Stardust Dragon!

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:22.030
There it is!

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:23.860
It's Yusei's ace monster!

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:25.120
It's cool!

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:31.460
But Stardust Dragon has fewer attack 
points than Ancient Gear Golem.

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.290
What is Yusei going to do?

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:40.950
That monster is no match against 
my three Ancient Gear Golems!

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:42.540
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:46.510
It's true that Stardust Dragon 
alone doesn't have the power

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:49.110
to destroy a single Ancient Gear Golem.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:52.220
But if it has the power 
of its many friends...

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:56.060
I activate the spell card 
Variety Comes Out from my hand!

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:58.420
By returning Stardust Dragon to my deck...

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:02.330
I can Special Summon Tuner 
Monsters from my graveyard

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:05.630
whose total Level equals 
Stardust Dragon's Level 8!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:06.860
What?

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:08.020
Resurrect!

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.730
Eccentric Boy!

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:10.570
Hanewata!

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:11.740
Debris Dragon!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:18.370
What are you thinking?

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:25.360
You got rid of a high-Level Synchro Monster 
to Special Summon low-Level Tuner Monsters?

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.320
No way!

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:30.140
That's right.

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:34.900
It's your so-called "garbage" 
monsters that are in their decks!

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:37.800
Here you go.

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:40.220
Sly, give him your card.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.040
Thank you.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:49.440
I promise to win with the 
cards you've lent me.

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.600
Yusei.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.020
Do your best, Yusei!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:52.640
Yusei!

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:57.430
You may have a lot of them, 
but they're still low Level!

00:18:57.430 --> 00:19:00.650
You can't destroy my high level combo!

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:03.820
Duels aren't solely decided 
by Levels or attack points!

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:06.150
I activate the trap Tuner's Explosion!

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:10.170
If I destroy the same number 
of monsters on my field

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:14.270
that you have on your field, all 
your monsters are destroyed!

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:16.700
What?  No way!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.280
Oh no!

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:31.680
My three Ancient Gear 
Golems were all destroyed!

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:37.750
For every destroyed monster, 
you take 1000 points of damage!

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.830
I still have a monster left!

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:46.800
Debris Dragon attacks you directly!

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:57.170
He did it!

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.840
Yusei won!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:03.060
Our monsters defeated the 
vice principal's monsters!

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.540
No way...

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:09.070
How could my victory deck lose?

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:13.310
I didn't know low-Level 
monsters had such potential.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.420
It's no surprise.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:17.760
High level isn't the most important thing.

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:20.620
It's the desire to learn!

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:25.650
These kids desire to learn about dueling!

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:27.700
Well said, Yusei.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:28.270
You're...

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:32.740
You tightened the screws, just as I asked.

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:34.380
Principal?

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:35.320
Principal?

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:38.750
I'm sorry to trick you, Yusei.

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:43.340
It was too hard for me 
to fix his stubbornness.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:47.780
Principal, you asked him to fix me?

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:50.460
Did it work, Vice Principal Heitmann?

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:53.950
Yes, I was wrong.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:55.700
Yusei!

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:58.070
These kids' expulsions are...

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.870
They're revoked.

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.870
Hooray!

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:04.870
Thank you, Yusei.

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:05.940
Thank you!

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:07.240
Thank you!

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:14.090
Zora, I can see why you expect 
great things from him.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:18.060
Yes, he has a mysterious power.

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:21.050
He can fix people's souls.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:28.510
Sly, thank you.

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.430
Thanks to your card, I won.

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:34.490
Yusei!

00:21:34.490 --> 00:21:35.590
Yusei!

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:40.380
He's lucky.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.670
I want it.

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:45.410
I want Stardust Dragon.

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:14.130
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:14.130 --> 00:22:19.130
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:24.040
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:29.040
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:29.230 --> 00:22:33.900
The cruel god tests us

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:40.840
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:44.710
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:50.580
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:50.750 --> 00:22:54.490
Bond is the proper word

00:22:54.490 --> 00:23:00.460
As we fight, we understand each other

00:23:00.460 --> 00:23:03.430
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:03.430 --> 00:23:05.670
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:10.340
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:13.210
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:13.210 --> 00:23:16.680
You want to party until the morning

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:19.910
At our special place
